================================================================================
LESSON 3: CREATE FOOTER COMPONENT IN REACT
================================================================================
LESSON OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This lesson covers how to:

- Create a reusable Footer component
- Keep Footer code separate from App.jsx
- Style the Footer using Bootstrap
- Import and use Footer in App.jsx
- Build a responsive Footer


================================================================================
1. WHAT IS A FOOTER COMPONENT?
================================================================================

A Footer is a UI section displayed at the bottom of a web page.

It commonly contains:

- Copyright information
- Navigation links
- Contact information
- Social media links
- Privacy and Terms links


Benefits:

- Reusable
- Maintainable
- Consistent
- Organized
- Scalable
- Separates Footer logic from App logic


================================================================================
2. WHY CREATE A SEPARATE FOOTER COMPONENT?
================================================================================

Without Components:
- Footer code may be duplicated
- Harder to maintain
- Pages may become inconsistent
- App.jsx becomes large

With Footer Component:
- One Footer can be reused everywhere
- Changes are made in one place
- Cleaner project structure
- Easier to add new Footer features


