ISSUE: FOOTER IS NOT AT THE BOTTOM OF A SHORT PAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Important:

mt-5 only adds margin above the Footer.

It does NOT guarantee that the Footer stays at the bottom of the viewport.

For a page with little content, use a flex layout.


App.jsx:

function App() {

  return (

    <div className="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100">

      <NavBar />

      <main className="container my-5 flex-grow-1">
        Main Content
      </main>

      <Footer />

    </div>

  );
}


Key Classes:

min-vh-100
-> Makes the layout at least the full viewport height

d-flex
-> Enables flexbox

flex-column
-> Arranges NavBar, content, and Footer vertically

flex-grow-1
-> Makes the main content use remaining available space


Result:

NavBar
   |
   v
Main Content
(expands)
   |
   v
Footer
(at bottom)


